e client sends Accept-Encoding: gzip. I enabled HTTP compression and added the OpenMetrics media type, but the response is still not compressed.\n\n```yaml\nquarkus:\n  http:\n    enable-compression: true\n    compress-media-types: application/openmetrics-text\n```\n\nRequest: \n```bash\ncurl -H \"Accept-Encoding: gzip\"  http://localhost:8081/q/metrics\n```\n\nCan someone help me understand why it’s not coming compressed?\nThanks in advance!\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWhen the client sends Accept-Encoding: gzip, the /q/metrics endpoint should return the response compressed (gzip), since HTTP compression is enabled and application/openmetrics-text is listed in the compressible media types.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nEven when the client sends Accept-Encoding: gzip, the /q/metrics response is returned uncompressed (plain text).\n\n### How to Reproduce?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Output of `uname -a` or `ver`\n\n_No response_\n\n### Output of `java -version`\n\n17.0.16\n\n### Quarkus version or git rev\n\n3.24.3\n\n### Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`)\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"brunobat","id":2318030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTgwMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2318030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobat","html_url":"https://github.com/brunobat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://a